+
+A call carries the change identity it sets when its change starts, and after each write and
+dispatch it reads whether the dropdown is live and whether a later `show` or `hide` call has
+started. A call that finds either stops, writing and dispatching nothing more, and resolves `false`.
+While a change is in flight every other call of the same dropdown resolves `false` at once, so a
+listener to the toggle's `focus` event that calls `hide` leaves the show to complete. A listener
+that shows or hides the menu inside the pre-change dispatch supersedes the call whose event it
+heard: a listener that shows the menu again inside `show.vn.dropdown` promotes it once and
+dispatches the one `shown.vn.dropdown` event, its own call resolves `true`, and the call whose event
+it heard resolves `false` and writes nothing. A listener that prevents the pre-change event starts
+no change, whatever else it wrote.
+
+The menu's `shown` token at the change's end is agreement. A host that adds the token before a show
+writes it, such as a listener to `show.vn.dropdown`, to the menu's opening `beforetoggle` event, or
+to the toggle's `focus` event, or removes it before a hide does, such as a listener to
+`hide.vn.dropdown` or to the menu's closing `beforetoggle` event, has made that write for the call.
+The call's token step writes the token only when the host has not, and the call completes every
+other write in its order, dispatches its completed event, and resolves `true`. From the moment the
+call finds the token at the change's end, right after the pre-change dispatch or at its own token
+step, each door also reads the token there, and a host that moves it back takes the change over.
+Until that moment a door reads only the call's identity and the dropdown's lifetime.
+
+A call the host took over resolves `false`, dispatches nothing, ends the change in flight, and takes
+one further step that returns what the change wrote to the state the host chose. The step reads no
+door; before each of its writes it reads only the call's identity and the dropdown's lifetime, so a
+destruction a reaction runs inside one stops the step, and a `show` or `hide` call a reaction starts
+inside one supersedes it. A show the host took over restores the placement, sets `aria-expanded` to
+`false`, and removes the toggle's `shown` token when the show had added it, as far as the show had
+written them. A hide the host took over adds the toggle's `shown` token back when the hide had
+removed it and sets `aria-expanded` to `true`, as far as the hide had written them. The placement
+the hide restored before its token step stays restored, because placing the menu again is an
+acquisition, so the menu shows in flow where the cascade puts it until the next hide.
+
+The dropdown passes its lifetime to the placement as the `signal` option, and the placement reads
+that signal after its `popover` attribute write and after the promotion, so a dropdown destroyed by
+the menu's `beforetoggle` event or by a reaction to that write leaves the placement restored and
+writing nothing more. Destruction closes an open menu without events, destroys the placement, and
+writes back the `shown` tokens of the menu and the toggle and the toggle's `aria-expanded` value. A
+`destroy` call made from a custom element's reaction to one of that restoration's own attribute
+writes, such as the menu's `popover` removal, completes the placement's restoration and the
+dropdown's before it returns, so no write of either lands after it.
+
+The platform closes the promoted menu when a `hide-popover` or `toggle-popover` invoker of yours, or
+your `hidePopover` call, aims at it. The dropdown reads that close from the menu's `toggle` event and
+hides the menu through its own sequence, dispatching `hide.vn.dropdown` and `hidden.vn.dropdown`
+with an undefined `click`; like light dismissal, that hide reads no disabled state. When a listener
+prevents that hide, the dropdown promotes the menu again, so it stays open and anchored. It does so
+once per placement: the platform's next close of the same shown menu hides it with
+`hide.vn.dropdown` dispatched and its prevention ignored.
 
